Software Requirements Specification (SRS)
Project: Skill Visibility Platform for Informal Workers
Target Region: Developing countries (initial pilot: Cameroon)
Version: 1.0

1. Introduction
1.1 Purpose
The platform aims to provide visibility for informal skill workers (e.g., carpenters, tailors, mechanics) by enabling them to showcase their skills, connect with potential clients, and access community resources. It will also log all searches and interactions for analytics to support decision-making by NGOs, policymakers, and community leaders.

1.2 Scope
Worker profiles with skill descriptions, photos, and endorsements.

Search functionality with logging for analytics.

Community features: announcements, events, and real estate listings.

Mobile-first, multilingual, and low-bandwidth friendly design.

1.3 Stakeholders
Primary Users: Informal workers, community members, employers.

Secondary Users: NGOs, policymakers, local government, researchers.

Administrators: Platform managers, moderators.

2. Functional Requirements
2.1 Worker Profiles
Create/edit profile with name, skill, location, contact info.

Upload photos/videos of work.

Endorsements and ratings from community members.

2.2 Search & Discovery
Search by skill, location, rating.

Filter results (e.g., “electricians in Douala”).

Log every search query and click for analytics.

2.3 Analytics Dashboard
Admin dashboard showing demand trends (e.g., “high demand for tailors in Yaoundé”).

Exportable reports (CSV, PDF).

Privacy controls for data use.

2.4 Community Features (Phase 2–3)
Announcements: Local job postings, training opportunities.

Events: Community workshops, fairs, skill showcases.

Real Estate: Listings for affordable housing and rental spaces.

3. Non-Functional Requirements
Performance: Fast response under low bandwidth.

Scalability: Support thousands of users across multiple regions.

Security: Data encryption, secure login, GDPR-like compliance.

Localization: French, English, and local languages.

Accessibility: Simple UI, mobile-first design.

4. System Architecture (High-Level)
Frontend: Mobile-first web app (React Native or Flutter).

Backend: RESTful API (Node.js/Express, Django, or similar).

Database: PostgreSQL/MySQL for structured data; ElasticSearch for search logging.

Analytics: Dashboard powered by Power BI or open-source alternatives.

5. Risks & Mitigation
Risk	Mitigation
Low digital literacy among workers	Provide training workshops, simple UI
Limited internet access	Offline caching, SMS-based features
Privacy concerns	Transparent consent, anonymized analytics
Scope creep	Phase-based rollout, clear prioritization
6. Roadmap
Phase 1: Worker profiles + search logging.

Phase 2: Analytics dashboard + community announcements/events.

Phase 3: Real estate listings + advanced features (recommendations, AI matching).


USER STORIES
Phase 1: Skill Visibility
Worker Profiles

As a worker, I want to create a profile with my name, skill, and location so that clients can find me.

As a worker, I want to upload photos/videos of my work so that clients can see proof of my skills.

As a community member, I want to endorse or rate a worker so that others can trust their skills.

Search & Discovery

As a client, I want to search for workers by skill and location so that I can quickly find someone nearby.

As a client, I want to filter search results by rating so that I can choose the most reliable worker.

As an administrator, I want every search query logged so that I can analyze demand trends.

🧩 Phase 2: Analytics & Decision-Making
As an administrator, I want to view a dashboard of search trends so that I can identify which skills are in high demand.

As an NGO, I want to export reports of worker demand so that I can design targeted training programs.

As a worker, I want to consent to how my data is used so that my privacy is protected.

🧩 Phase 3: Community Features
Announcements

As a community leader, I want to post announcements so that workers are informed about opportunities.

As a worker, I want to see announcements relevant to my skill so that I don’t miss important updates.

Events

As an organizer, I want to post community events so that workers can attend skill showcases or workshops.

As a worker, I want to RSVP to events so that I can participate and network.

Real Estate

As a landlord, I want to list affordable housing or workshop spaces so that workers can find places to live or work.

As a worker, I want to search for real estate listings so that I can secure housing or workspace.

🧩 Non-Functional Stories
As a user, I want the platform to work on low bandwidth so that I can access it even with poor internet.

As a user, I want the platform available in French, English, and local languages so that I can use it in my preferred language.

As a user, I want a simple mobile-first interface so that I can easily navigate without technical training.

